  "source": "EAMCET 2008 (Medical)",
  "question": "A charge $Q$ is placed at each corner of a cube of side $a$. The potential at the centre of the cube is",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{8Q}{\\pi\\epsilon_0 a}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{4Q}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0 a}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{4Q}{\\sqrt{3}\\,\\pi\\epsilon_0 a}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{2Q}{\\pi\\epsilon_0 a}$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "C",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "Each corner is at $\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}a}{2}$ from the centre. Potentials add as scalars:\n$$V = 8 \\times \\frac{Q}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0}\\cdot\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}a} = \\frac{4Q}{\\sqrt{3}\\,\\pi\\epsilon_0 a}$$",
